course: dictionary
lesson: 121
title: Adrenaline: the body's alarm
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Adrenaline is a chemical your body makes when you feel scared, excited or in danger. It is a hormone, a messenger that tells the body to speed up. «Straight after a match your body is still full of adrenaline» means the chemical is still working for a while after the excitement.
explain: Adrenaline helps with «fight or flight». When danger comes, the body gets ready to fight or run away: the heart beats faster, you breathe quicker and you get quick energy. That is why you may feel butterflies in your tummy before a big test or a race.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentences. «Anger and excitement release adrenaline, which speeds up the heart and wakes the brain.» The words speeds up and wakes show that adrenaline makes the body more alert, not calmer. «It takes time to calm down» tells you the effect does not stop straight away.
explain: Adrenaline is also a medicine, sometimes called epinephrine. People with a severe allergy may carry an adrenaline pen. «Call the emergency number at once and help the person use their adrenaline pen.» In an emergency, call for help straight away and always tell a grown-up.
fact: Adrenaline is a hormone, a chemical that carries messages around the body.
fact: Your body releases adrenaline when you are scared, excited or in danger.
fact: Adrenaline makes your heart beat faster and gives you quick energy.
fact: «Fight or flight» is the body's way of getting ready to fight or run away from danger.
fact: Adrenaline is also used as a medicine, in an adrenaline pen, for people with a severe allergic reaction called anaphylaxis.
exercise: In the sentence «Straight after a match your body is still full of adrenaline», what does adrenaline mean? | A part of the body that helps you see | A type of fizzy drink for athletes | *A chemical your body releases when you are scared, excited or in danger | A kind of food eaten before a match
exercise: «Fight or flight» means the body gets ready to... | Eat a big meal | Play a quiet game indoors | Sleep for a long time | *Fight or run away from danger
exercise: Which of these is a sign that adrenaline is working in your body? | Feeling bored and calm | A slower heartbeat | Yawning and feeling sleepy | *A faster heartbeat
test: Adrenaline is used in an emergency pen for people with a severe allergy. What is the best first step if someone has a bad allergic reaction? | Give them a cold drink and let them sleep | *Call the emergency number and help them use their adrenaline pen | Wait and see if it passes by itself | Tell them to calm down and stop worrying
test: Mason smashed his racket after losing 6–2. Why might his body be full of adrenaline? | *He was excited and angry, which releases adrenaline | He had won the match 6–2 | He was eating his dinner | He was fast asleep
exam: Which word from «Anger and excitement release adrenaline, which speeds up the heart and wakes the brain» shows that adrenaline makes the body more alert? | slows | hides | calms | *wakes
